          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "2.1 A Quick Recap of Integers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.333,
            0.482,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": "Rakesh’s Puzzle: A Number Game"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.367,
            0.595,
            0.438
          ],
          "content": "Rakesh gives you a challenge. “I have thought of two numbers”, he says. “Their **sum is 25**, and their **difference is 11**.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.451,
            0.492,
            0.473
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Can you tell me the two numbers?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.477,
            0.846,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "You don’t need to use any formulas. Just try different pairs of numbers and then check:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.515,
            0.537,
            0.534
          ],
          "content": "1. Do the two numbers add up to 25?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.535,
            0.545,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": "2. Is the difference between them 11?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.552,
            0.793,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "(Remember: the difference means first number – second number.) Write your guesses like this:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.602,
            0.844,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": "| First Number | Second Number | Sum | Difference |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 10 | 15 | 25 | -5 |\n| 20 | 5 | 25 | 15 |\n| 19 | 6 | 25 | 13 |\n| 18 | 7 | 25 | 11 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_table_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.746,
            0.422,
            0.77
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Did you find the right pair?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.783,
            0.846,
            0.824
          ],
          "content": "? Now that you’ve found the correct pair, Rakesh gives you a second challenge:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.833,
            0.829,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": "“Think of two numbers whose **sum is 25**, but their **difference is –11**.”"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.858,
            0.847,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": "Use the same method. Try different pairs of numbers and fill in the table again. You will notice that if you swap the numbers from the first"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
